Specifies whether the IFC loader will use its own, custom triangulation algorithm to triangulate wall and floor meshes. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
If this property is set to false, walls will be either triangulated by {\b aiProcess_Triangulate} or will be passed through as huge polygons with faked holes (i.e. holes that are connected with the outer boundary using a dummy edge). It is highly recommended to set this property to true if you want triangulated data because {\b aiProcess_Triangulate} is known to have problems with the kind of polygons that the IFC loader spits out for complicated meshes. Property type: Bool. Default value: true. \par
}}
