\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Defines the begin of the time range for which the LWS loader evaluates animations and computes {\b aiNodeAnim}'s. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
{\b Assimp} provides full conversion of LightWave's envelope system, including pre and post conditions. The loader computes linearly subsampled animation chanels with the frame rate given in the LWS file. This property defines the start time. Note: animation channels are only generated if a node has at least one envelope with more tan one key assigned. This property. is given in frames, '0' is the first frame. By default, if this property is not set, the importer takes the animation start from the input LWS file ('FirstFrame' line)\par
 Property type: Integer. Default value: taken from file.\par
{{\s5\sb90\sa30\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs16\cgrid 
