\par
{
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Specify the Quake 3 shader file to be used for a particular MD3 file. This can also be a search path. }}\par
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
By default {\b Assimp}'s behaviour is as follows: If a MD3 file {\f2 any_path/models/any_q3_subdir/model_name/file_name.md3}  is loaded, the library tries to locate the corresponding shader file in {\f2 any_path/scripts/model_name.shader} . This property overrides this behaviour. It can either specify a full path to the shader to be loaded or alternatively the path (relative or absolute) to the directory where the shaders for all MD3s to be loaded reside. {\b Assimp} attempts to open {\f2 IMPORT_MD3_SHADER_SRC/model_name.shader}  first, {\f2 IMPORT_MD3_SHADER_SRC/file_name.shader}  is the fallback file. Note that IMPORT_MD3_SHADER_SRC should have a terminal (back)slash. Property type: String. Default value: n/a. \par
}}
